  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129500/assets/7476c8699798c46fa643ec6c4d87d01056aef9581fa02a02cbc38ac46a06005a.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the multiplication problem above?",
  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{1}{4}$ on the left and $\\frac{3}{4}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129500/assets/9992a38b2966e0f3cfd28c32c269c8acc0db00e443cf57783545fdf38f5f7ef9.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $1$ shaded piece, and the shape on the right has $3$ shaded pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $3.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\times 3=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $3.$",
